n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-2 (-2)+5=4+5=9 \\\\ y & =-2 (-2)^{3}+2 (-2)=16-4=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we're looking to find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point $(9,12).$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we need to find $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$ To compute it, we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx'(t)=-2,\\qquad y'(t)=-6 t^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}=\\frac{-6 t^{2}+2}{-2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-2,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{-6 (-2)^{2}+2}{-2}=\\frac{-22}{-2}=11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the equation of the tangent line, we use point-slope form with the point $(x_1,y_1)=(9,12)$ and the slope $m=11.$ We get\n\n$$\ny-12=11(x-9).\n$$" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553824 1080 "y-3=-\\frac{3}{7}(x-2)" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553824 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553824 1083 #uuid "82675b58-ae0e-59ed-a375-557f1aa20546" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553825 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553838 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553825 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553825 1071 "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2 t+1,\\qquad y=2 t^{3}+3 t,\\qquad -\\infty<t<\\infty.\n$$\n\nCalculate the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=-2.$" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553825 1072 #uuid "8479a10a-7f66-540d-8458-dda374fac829" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553825 1074 "First, we find the coordinates of the point by substituting $t=-2$ into the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2 (-2)+1=-4+1=-3 \\\\ y & =2 (-2)^{3}+3 (-2)=-16-6=-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we're looking to find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point $(-3,-22).$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we need to find $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.$ To compute it, we first need to find the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx'(t)=2,\\qquad y'(t)=6 t^{2}+3.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}=\\frac{6 t^{2}+3}{2}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=-2,$ the slope of the tangent line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{6 (-2)^{2}+3}{2}=\\frac{27}{2}=\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate the equation of the tangent line, we use point-slope form with the point $(x_1,y_1)=(-3,-22)$ and the slope $m=\\frac{27}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\ny+22=\\frac{27}{2}(x+3).\n$$" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553826 1080 "y-22=\\frac{27}{2}(x+3)" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553826 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553826 1083 #uuid "8a92aeb3-1beb-54cc-b477-c93cbea1b51d" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553814 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553819 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553821 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553822 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553834 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1077 "selection" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553821 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553827 1079 #uuid "8d58c371-70ac-58e2-a830-97e519cbae19" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553828 1080 "y+3=-\\frac{7}{3}(x-2)" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553828 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535994 17592186045443 true] [17592186553828 1083 #uuid "9dab7e5a-245a-5e90-968a-9b67cfdbad83" 13194139535994 17592186045443 true]